⚠️ **IMPORTANT: `_resolveCodeMieProject` can report a DIFFERENT project than the one the model requests bill**

The doc comment claims "the quota fetch must name the SAME project the model requests bill", but the implementation is a first-match scan over **all** saved entries:

1. **Multi-entry divergence** — with two saved CodeMie entries carrying different projects (e.g. the gh-1000 twin-account setup, or two orgs), the quota fetch reports the first entry's project while the live model may bill the other one. The exact display/billing divergence this PR forbids.
2. **No endpoint filter** — the sibling resolver right above (`_resolveCodeMieSessionCookie`) only considers entries whose `baseUrl` contains `/code-assistant-api/`; this one accepts `project:` from ANY entry, so a hand-edited `project:` on a non-CodeMie custom entry leaks onto the CodeMie quota request.

Suggested fix — prefer the live model's header, fall back to a filtered scan:

```dart
String? _resolveCodeMieProject() {
  final live = _agent.state.model.codeMieProject;
  if (live != null) return live;
  for (final entry in config.customProviders?.entries ?? const []) {
    if (!entry.baseUrl.contains('/code-assistant-api/')) continue;
    if (entry.project != null) return entry.project;
  }
  return null;
}
```

(Resolvers are closures invoked per fetch, so this stays live across `/model` and `/provider` switches. The PR description's "wired to the first saved entry carrying a project" acknowledges the simplification, but the in-code contract comment promises parity the code doesn't deliver.)
